   "source": [
    "## 7. Classification Model\n",
    "\n",
    "A Logistic Regression baseline — simple, fast, and its coefficients double as a business explanation later. Features are scaled first since Logistic Regression is sensitive to feature scale."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "8a89c7dc",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-08T08:33:32.566650Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-08T08:33:32.566528Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-08T08:33:32.577054Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-08T08:33:32.576325Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Model trained on 800 customers\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "scaler = StandardScaler()                          # will rescale each column to mean 0, std 1\n",
    "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)      # learn the scaling from train, and apply it\n",
    "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)            # apply the SAME scaling to test (never re-fit on test)\n",
    "\n",
    "model = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, random_state=42)\n",
    "model.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
    "print(\"Model trained on\", X_train.shape[0], \"customers\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2a66c827",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "Accuracy alone would be misleading here given the 88/12 class split, so Precision, Recall and the Confusion Matrix are reported alongside it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "0d615d2c",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-08T08:33:32.578724Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-08T08:33:32.578242Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-08T08:33:32.588478Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-08T08:33:32.587753Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Accuracy:  0.965\n",
      "Precision: 0.962\n",
      "Recall:    1.000\n",
      "F1-score:  0.981\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "y_pred = model.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "acc = accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred)         # overall % correct\n",
    "prec = precision_score(y_test, y_pred)       # trustworthiness of a \"will churn\" prediction\n",
    "rec = recall_score(y_test, y_pred)           # % of real churners the model actually caught\n",
    "f1 = f1_score(y_test, y_pred)                # balance of precision and recall\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Accuracy:  {acc:.3f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Precision: {prec:.3f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Recall:    {rec:.3f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"F1-score:  {f1:.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
