  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1a0d04d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Reading the result — and being skeptical of it.** 100% recall on churners is unusually clean for a churn model; real customer behavior is noisier than this. It suggests `TechSupport` and `ContractType` are close to a deterministic rule for churn in this particular dataset, rather than the messier signal you'd see in production. The one real weak spot: recall on the minority **No Churn** class is only 70% — 7 loyal customers were incorrectly flagged as churn risks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "edf3cc9a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Business Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
